      "text": "I've marked the run as UNKNOWN and flagged it for a human to review. The sensors that are installed look normal, but the growth stage needs an exhaust O2 reading to confirm the atmosphere is inert, and this furnace doesn't have that sensor.\n\n- **Temperature:** the ramp followed setpoint closely. The growth hold is steady at 749.9 °C against 750 °C, after a brief overshoot to 760.3 °C at t=2520 s.\n- **Heater power:** steady at about 46% during the hold, which matches the temperature reading.\n- **Argon flow:** on setpoint, 100.7 sccm against 100 sccm.\n- **Pressure:** flat at about 760 Torr the whole run. Since the tube is at atmospheric pressure, a small leak letting air in wouldn't show up here, so pressure alone can't rule out oxygen getting in.\n\nNo sample has been characterized yet, so there's no evidence either way on whether the material grew. Two things would settle the atmosphere question: an oxygen measurement on the exhaust with a portable analyzer, or a pressure-decay leak test on the sealed tube."
     }
